---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_UPDATED } from '../lib/site';
---

<Prose
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Vanishnote's privacy policy: what we collect, how long we keep it, and what we never collect at all."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  lead={`Last updated ${LEGAL_UPDATED}. We built Vanishnote to collect as little as possible. This page explains the little we do handle.`}
>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>
    Notes are encrypted in your browser before they reach us. We store the encrypted data, its settings (expiry, views
    remaining, whether a password was used) and the time it was created. We cannot decrypt notes. Each note is deleted
    when its last allowed view happens, when it expires, or when you use its destroy link. Expired notes are removed
    within an hour.
  </p>

  <h2>Email addresses</h2>
  <p>
    If you ask to be notified when a note is read, we store your email address with that note and use it only to send
    that notification. It is deleted together with the note. We send notification emails through our email provider,
    Resend, which processes your address only to deliver the message.
  </p>

  <h2>Technical data</h2>
  <p>
    Like every website, we receive your IP address and basic request information when you use Vanishnote. We use your
    IP address briefly for rate limiting to prevent abuse, and we do not store it or log it. We have turned off request
    logging on our hosting platform so note links are not recorded.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, names or phone numbers.</li>
    <li>No cookies, advertising identifiers or tracking pixels.</li>
    <li>No third-party analytics, fonts or scripts.</li>
    <li>Never your note's text, its key, or its password.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p>
    Vanishnote runs on Cloudflare's network (hosting and database). Read notifications are delivered by Resend. Both act
    on our behalf and only handle the data described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we hold no accounts and delete data on a short schedule, there is usually nothing we can link to you. If you
    have a question or request about your data, contact <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
</Prose>
